# S4: hand the cards back. This is the LAST job of the window and it runs even when a stop job halted the window and after a stall or a hang in any arm, which can leave all four cards hung
# with production down: the status of every board, the all-four reset, the fabric re-measure and the node agent started again. Then the OWNER runs the deploy (/deploy) that places TODAY'S PRODUCTION
# RECIPE (the thin layer image the rig daemon :latest already names: profile c2-packed-tp4 with the verify audits off and the pinned sampler in the verify trace, QWEN_FAST_PACKED_SAMPLER_IN_TRACE=1);
# that deploy is never part of this job file and needs the owner go-ahead and an admin token. NEVER place a gate arm: not a tpub arm, not a best arm, not any gate-only profile, and not
# this window's image. No :latest retag unless a new image was chosen. Pass: all four boards enumerate after the reset, the fabric re-measure passes, the agent is up, then /v1/models answers
# Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B:tt and a chat completes on the placed endpoint. If the reset does not heal a board after a stall, production stays down until it does.
# Duration (estimate): 25 min. Stop rule: any failure stops the window (it is the last job).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/tpub window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/tpub and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1 is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset fabric agentstart
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
